-- title:
--   A finite-type equivariant affine neighbourhood of an end
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ are primes with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. The field $L$ has characteristic $0$, $\xi\in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is pinned by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and subgroup $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The base ring $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\xi$ in the image of $A$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j\in K$ has Laurent series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (the normalised $j$-expansion $q^{-1}+\dots$) and is nonzero; $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$, and $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ with $u$ a unit. Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A ↥K j` $=j$, and $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart into $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and into $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the corresponding algebra built from $j^{-1}$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and canonical morphism `ιFin` from `XFin` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$. The ideal $y\subset C$ is maximal, contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the rigidified Drinfeld-chart input at all supersingular points above $\varpi$: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` mapping $y'$ to $z$ and with $y'$ supersingular in the sense above, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu)$, such that, with `toC` the completion map, `mkS` the quotient map and `germY` the canonical map $C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ coming from `ιFin` at $y'$, the following seven clauses hold: (i) $e$ sends the germ of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ acts on quotients $f/g$ of weight-$k$ modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions by the action of the matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` on $q$-expansions, read through any embedding $\iota$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$ — the subalgebra $C$ is $\tau$-stable; (iii) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in\mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $\tau$ through $e\circ$`toC`$\circ$`germY`; $\theta$ fixing the classes of constants; $\theta(X_{j})\equiv\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$; $c\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c\not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element congruent to $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e\circ$`toC` differ; (vi) for such a prime $P$ with direction $(1,0)$, an element $a\in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference in $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, such that $e$ carries the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   Next a particular point is fixed: $z$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ above $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y` identifying $y'$ with $y$. Data $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ of the shape produced by `hArig` are given, with $W_1$ a complete discrete valuation ring, $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, $u_1,v_1$ units, $f_1\equiv$ `drinfeldForm q W₁` modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and $e_1$ an isomorphism of the completed stalk at $z$ with $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this witness exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   The ideal $J\subset C$ is pinned by `hJ` to be the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\mathrm{comap}$ along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ$`toC`$\circ$`germY` of the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving $C$. The subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is pinned by `hB` to be $C[J/\varpi_t]$, the $A$-subalgebra generated over $C$ by the $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$. A valuation subring $W\subseteq K$ is given with $B\subseteq W$ (`hBW`), together with: `hR1`, that $C\le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W\cap L$ is the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ membership in $y$ is equivalent to membership in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms through elements $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains a level translate of $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$; that an element of $B$ all of whose level translates by $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that $W$ is stable under any level automorphism that preserves $y$ on $C$.
--
--   Finally the end is given: a subring $O\subseteq K$ such that (`hO`) for some $a\in J$ with $a\neq0$ in $K$ and $B_a=C[J/a]$ there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ equal to the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, with every element of $y$ a non-unit in $O$ whenever it lies in $O$, and with $B$ not contained in $O$; moreover $O\subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C$ is contained in $O$ (`hCO`). The hypothesis `hIgStab` requires that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V\cap L$ the image of $A$, with $\varpi\in\mathfrak m_V$, containing $C$, and admitting some $c\in C$ such that $p(c)$ lies in $V$ and outside $\mathfrak m_V$ for every monic $p\in A[X]$, is stable under every level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists an $A$-subalgebra $B_x\subseteq K$ with the following five properties. First, $B_x$ is contained in $B$ and in $O$. Second, $B_x$ is of finite type over $A$. Third, $B_x$ is stable under every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$. Fourth, $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its elements which are units in $O$: an element $f\in K$ lies in $O$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h$ lies in $O$. Fifth, $B_x$ detects the failure of $O$ to be contained in a valuation subring: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is the image of $A$, such that $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$ whenever it lies in $V$, and such that $j\in V$ and $p(j)\notin\mathfrak m_V$ for every monic $p\in A[X]$ with $p(j)\in V$, if some element of $O$ is not in $V$ then some element of $B_x$ is not in $V$.
--
--   This is the construction of an affine, level-equivariant neighbourhood of an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart along the weighted centre $J$: a finite-type $A$-algebra $B_x$ inside $B\cap O$ which localises to the local ring $O$ of the end and is stable under the automorphisms coming from $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, together with a valuative separation property. It feeds the next step, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), in the analysis of the local structure of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ at its supersingular points.
